win32u: Implement NtGdiDdDDIOpenAdapterFromHdc and NtGdiDdDDIWaitForVerticalBlankEvent.

Both were stubs (STATUS_NO_MEMORY, and an unimplemented syscall that gdi32 did not even
export), so code pacing itself on vblank, such as Chromium's GPU vsync thread, had to fall
back. OpenAdapterFromHdc uses the DC's display (or the primary one) and the GDI display
name path; the wait returns at the next refresh of the current mode, as DwmFlush does.
Test: wine/tests/vblank/vblank.c (64- and 32-bit).

